BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 748.0 Td (        and watch what blooms.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (      The Northern elder was afraid. "If we give our water away, we'll have nothing.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (      But a young woman stepped forward. "Trust," she said, pouring one bucket into the valley. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (        Miraculously, it became three buckets by the time it reached the South.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (      The Southern village rejoiced. Their elder declared, "This gift must be honored!" They ret) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (        urned two buckets to the North.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (      Now both villages had more than before. The cycle continued-each act of giving multiplied,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (         each return honored the trust. The valley between them transformed into flowering garde) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (        ns that fed both peoples.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (      But the goddess warned: "This magic lives only when both give freely and return generously) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (        . Hoard, and the wells run dry. Break trust, and the desert returns.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (      The villages prospered for generations, understanding that abundance flows not from graspi) Tj ET
