BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 748.0 Td (    Ninth dusk arrived-the Dusk of Triple Completion. The Southern Keeper prepared to cast beaco) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (      ns. A young sailor asked: "Keeper, after nine perfect exchanges, do you ever wonder if you) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (       could keep more?") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (    The Southern Keeper gazed at the endless waves: *"After nine tides, there is no 'could.' Nin) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (      e is three threes-completion cubed, stability absolute. The question you ask dissolved nin) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (      e tides ago. I don't cast all five beacons because I'm generous or strategic. I cast them ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (      because a wave cannot choose not to wave, a lighthouse cannot choose not to shine. We have) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (       become the tide itself."*) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (    All five beacons crossed the waters. Fifteen lights blazed back.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (    The Moon Spirit's voice rolled through the waves: *"Nine tides have transformed intention in) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (      to instinct, choice into nature. You are no longer players of a game-you are the game play) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (      ing itself. Perfect reciprocity breathes through you like wind through open windows. Conti) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (      nue not because you should, but because you cannot be otherwise. The tide is eternal."*) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (  Agent_2 \(Briar\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (    Myth: In the Garden of Eternal Cycles, two Gardeners tended the Tree of Perfect Balance. Eac) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (      h season, one would plant five sacred seeds in blessed soil. The Growth Spirit would multi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (      ply them to fifteen blooms, and the receiving Gardener chose what to harvest back.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
